te notes grounded in evidence, I need evidence ids. I can recall evidence ids for pages I read.\n\nLet me first print key pages to find answers. Since content is in memory, printing is fine (but must be careful of output budget; keep to relevant excerpts).\n\nStrategy: find answers:\n1. overview: categories = reason, act, interact; search_methods: Google Scholar \"Agentic LLM\" then snowballing. Page 5.\n2. reasoning: Self Consistency selection rule (majority vote / most consistent answer), ToT search controllers (BFS and DFS). Page ~10.\n3. tool_use: Toolformer five tools: calculator, question answering, machine translation, web search, calendar. ToolBench API count (16,464?). Page ~21-24.\n4. multi_agent: CAMEL prompting = role-playing with inception prompting (\"inception prompting\"). Generative Agents evaluators count (?) maybe 100? Page ~40-44.\n5. outlook: Table 4 five topics; conclusion shared foundations = reflection and retrieval? Actually likely \"reasoning and reflection\"? Need to check page 52.\n\nLet me grep the pages list for keywords."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7792, "completion_tokens": 643, "total_tokens": 8435, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4224}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 482}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4224, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 3568}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
