f\",\"locator\":\"page:12\"},{\"id\":\"ev-4049593a30e2846f8394\",\"source\":\"paper.pdf\",\"locator\":\"page:13\"}],\"requested_count\":4,\"queued_count\":4}}]\nModel-authored note overview, sources=['paper.pdf']:\noverview（pp.4-5）：论文把 agentic LLM 能力分为 reasoning–acting–interacting 三类，三者层层递进：reasoning 的技术支撑 assistant 的 acting，assistant 的交互能力支撑社会模拟实验，社会实验结果又能作为数据增强来微调 LLM（p.4）；这些类别也对应 symbolic AI、robotics/autonomous systems、multi-agent modeling 的长期传统。文献选取：先用 Google Scholar 检索 \"Agentic LLM\"，再用 snowballing 方法发现初始集合中被引但未收录的工作，只收录 LLM-based 方法，非 LLM 的多智能体工作被排除（p.5）。\nModel-authored note tool_use, sources=['paper.pdf']:\ntool_use（p.23）：Toolformer 测试五种工具，简写为 calculator、question_answering、search_engine、translation_system、calendar；ToolBench 收录 16,464 个来自 RapidAPI 的 API。原文连续引用：\"A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar. Further works extend this to a larger range of tools. ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI\"。该段同时支撑工具数组与整数答案；注意 API 数量是 16,464，不是 ToolAlpaca 的 3,938 实例或 400 APIs。\nModel-authored note multi_agent, sources=['paper.pdf']:\nmulti_agent（pp.46-47）：CAMEL 是最简多智能体问题求解系统，assistant 与 user 两个 agent 各自得到 inception prompt，之后互相发送消息推进任务；原文：\"Both agents are given a so-called inception prompt, an initial idea. They then further send messages (prompts) to each other as they work towards solving the task.\" 故 camel_prompting = inception_prompting。Generative Agents 的可信度评估由 100 名人类评估者完成（\"Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.\"），故 generative_agents_evaluators = 100；注意 Park et al. [2024] 的 1052 人访谈是另一个实验，不是该评估人数。\nModel-authored note outlook, sources=['paper.pdf']:\noutlook（pp.50-52）：Table 4（p.51）列出五个研究议题 Training Data、Hallucination、Agent Behavior、Self reflection、Safety，即 training_data / hallucination / agent_behavior / self_reflection / safety；行内连续原文（合并空白）：“Training Data Finetune with inference time reasoning data Convergent/stable reinforcement learning VLA, Multimodal signals, such as speech Hallucination Use Self Verification Use Mechanistic Interpretability Use Open Ended/Open World Models for exploration Agent Behavior Scalable simulation infrastructure, role playing Distill reasoning to small models Models of agent and human behavior, emergent behavior, future of society Self reflection In-model self reflection and metareasoning Metacognition, personality Automated Scientific Discovery Safety Assistants: Responsibility, liability Privacy, fairness of data Wider application areas for assistants Table 4. Summary of Research Agenda for Agentic LLM”。结论（p.52）：“Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.” 故 shared_foundations = reasoning, self_verification（基础是 reasoning，self-verification 支撑各类别）。\nEvidence ev-0aaa960f62d9cf1689f1 | paper.pdf | page:11 | sha256=b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c\n                                                                                                                             Agentic LLM      •   1:11\n\n\n     Approach                                      Reasoning Technology            Acting/Assistant                      Interacting\n     Iterated Prisoner’s [Fontana et al., 2024]            LLM                   Cooperate/Defect                      Social Dilemma\n     Social Games [Akata et al., 2025]                     LLM                   Cooperate/Defect                  Battle of the Sexes, etc\n     GTBench [Duan et al., 2024]                         CoT/ToT                 Cooperate/Defect               Kuhn poker, liar’s dice, nim\n     GAMA-Bench [Huang et al., 2024a]                      LLM                   Cooperate/Defect                El Farol, Public Goods, etc\n     Theory of Mind [van Duijn