l output size: maybe 3000 chars, acceptable.\n\nLet me do it.\n\nCode:\n\nimport json\nres = read_file('report.json')\nprint('REPORT:', res['content'][:500], res['file_hash'])\n\ndef get(s,e):\n    r = run_command(argv=[\"python\",\"read_pdf.py\",\"--start-page\",str(s),\"--end-page\",str(e)])\n    return json.loads(r['stdout'])['pages']\n\npages = get(4,5)\nfor p in pages: print('P%d'%p['page'], p['text'][:...]) \n\nBetter to print targeted regex matches:\n\nimport re\ndef snips(text, kws, width=400):\n    out=[]\n    for kw in kws:\n        for m in re.finditer(kw, text, re.I):\n            out.append(text[max(0,m.start()-200):m.start()+width])\n    return out\n\nI'll print unique.\n\nLet's do pages 4-5 with keywords 'categor|three|reasoning, acting'. Hmm page 4 text maybe contains \"We categorize the abilities of agentic LLMs into reasoning, acting, and interacting\". Keyword 'interacting'.\n\nPage 10-11: 'Self Consistency|self-consistency|majority|Tree of Thoughts|breadth|depth'.\n\nPage 23: 'Toolformer|ToolBench'.\n\nPage 46-47: 'inception|CAMEL|human evaluators|Generative Agents'.\n\nPage 50-52: 'Table 4|Research Agenda|benefit from'.\n\nPrint each snippet trimmed to ~600 chars.\n\nLet's write.\n\nActually run_command is a tool function callable in action code? Yes, \"Call tools with keyword arguments\" and examples show run_command in code blocks. Good.\n\nI'll do one command per page range, that's fine.\n\nOutput budget: 5 ranges * few snippets. Keep each snippet 500 chars, max ~10 snippets = 5000 chars. Acceptable-ish. Let me limit.\n\nLet me be more surgical: just print full text of the specific pages? Pages are ~4000 chars each; too much. Use regex windows.\n\nGo."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 9010, "completion_tokens": 2766, "total_tokens": 11776, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4352}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 2367}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4352, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens